   "text": {
    "L1": "An angle measures how much something turns, not how long its arms are.",
    "L2": "So the longer arms in this myth do not make the angle bigger.",
    "L3": "A full turn brings you back to where you started.",
    "L4": "A quarter turn is one right angle, and four quarter turns make a full turn.",
    "L5": "A half turn is two quarter turns, so you face the opposite way.",
    "L6": "Three quarter turns are three quarter turns of a full turn.",
    "L7": "Clockwise follows clock hands; anticlockwise goes the other way.",
    "L8": "Now check: how many quarter turns make a half turn?"
   },
